# Cubed sphere, MHD: the MANUFACTURED SOLUTION of Ivan, De Sterck, Northrup & Groth
# (JCP 2013, sect. 5.2.1, eqs 11-12).  Build with -D PROBLEM=cs_test.  layoutaudit-1103.
#
#   rho = p = r^-5/2,  v = r^1/2 rhat + kappa r^5/2 zhat,  B = rhat/r^2 + kappa zhat
# (eq 11 lists PRIMITIVES [rho, v, B, p]); v x B = 0 and B is curl free.  It is steady
# with the eq 12 source Q_O on momentum and energy (checked by finite differences: eq 12
# is exact as printed, and gamma independent).  Shell r = 2..3.5, kappa = 0.017,
# gamma 1.4; supersonic (fast) everywhere, v_r - c_f ~ 0.07 at the inner boundary, so the
# initial transient flushes slowly: tlim = 10.  Faces: monopole as 1/r_f^2 on the radial
# faces (flux = exact solid angle), kappa zhat as the discrete curl of
# A = kappa/2 zhat x r; div B is round-off.  Inner radial ghosts exact; outer ghosts:
# conserved variables extrapolated linearly, faces exact.  Outputs as cs_ivan_hyd.
# Radial cells = 1.25 x nx2 (the paper's 8x8x10 ... grids):
#   for n in 8 16 32 64; do athena -i cs_ivan_mhd.athinput mesh/nx1=$((5*n/4)) ...; done
# RESULT 11-03 (CPU athena_cpu_cs_test_iv1, plm/hlld/rk2, cfl 0.3, tlim 10, extend):
#   nx2  nx1      L1        L2       Linf     orders L1 / L2 / Linf   seam/int (mean L1)
#     8   10   1.961e-4  2.111e-4  3.487e-4                           0.80
#    16   20   4.710e-5  4.928e-5  8.792e-5   2.06 / 2.10 / 1.99      0.87
#    32   40   1.155e-5  1.193e-5  2.310e-5   2.03 / 2.05 / 1.93      0.96
#    64   80   2.858e-6  2.934e-6  6.542e-6   2.01 / 2.02 / 1.82      1.00
# The ring profile is flat (C64: 2.83e-6 .. 2.93e-6 for rings d = 0 .. 30, 3.13e-6 at the
# panel centre), so the seam is not worse than the interior.  The Linf order drops
# because the maximum sits on the +z POLAR panel (panel 3), a few cells off the axis,
# near the inner boundary, where v_r and B_r have a tangential extremum.  It is not at a
# seam.  Likely cause (NOT verified): the van Leer PLM slope goes to zero at an extremum.
# ppm4 (nghost 3) is no cure.  Its L1 is the same as plm (1.96e-4 / 4.70e-5 / 1.15e-5),
# but its C32 Linf is 3.41e-5 ON THE SEAM ring (seam/int max ratio 1.43; Linf orders
# 1.91 / 1.46).
# GATE (USER 11-03): L1 and L2 order >= 1.95 (PASS: 2.01 / 2.02 at C32 -> C64); Linf is
# reported only, or >= 1.8 (1.82 here, off the seams at a tangential extremum: limiter
# clipping, generic); the seam ring must be no worse than the interior (PASS).
# AXES: x1 is RADIAL; x2 = xi and x3 = eta are the panel-tangential angles.

<comment>
problem = cubed sphere MHD manufactured solution (Ivan et al. 2013)

<job>
basename = cs_ivan_mhd

<mesh>
nghost   = 2
nx1      = 20
x1min    = 2.0
x1max    = 3.5
ix1_bc   = user
ox1_bc   = user
nx2      = 16
x2min    = -1.0
x2max    = 1.0
ix2_bc   = panel
ox2_bc   = panel
nx3      = 16
x3min    = -1.0
x3max    = 1.0
ix3_bc   = panel
ox3_bc   = panel
use_cubed_sphere = true
cs_seam_blockend = extend

<meshblock>
nx1      = 20
nx2      = 16
nx3      = 16

<time>
evolution  = dynamic
integrator = rk2
cfl_number = 0.3
nlim       = -1
tlim       = 10.0     # L1rho flat to 0.3 % from t ~ 5 (slowest radial crossing 6.4)
ndiag      = 1000

<mhd>
eos         = ideal
reconstruct = plm
rsolver     = hlld
gamma       = 1.4

<problem>
iprob     = 18
kappa     = 0.017
ivan_outer_exact = 0
user_srcs = true
user_hist = true

<output1>
file_type = hst
dt        = 0.5
